---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for christran.io and associated services"
>
	<p><em>Last updated: June 13, 2026</em></p>

	<p>
		This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>christran.io</strong> collects, uses, and discloses your personal information 
		when you visit our site or use our associated web applications (including <a href="https://synx.christran.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sYnX</a>, <a href="https://illusyn.christran.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">illusYn</a>, and other subdomains).
	</p>

	<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>
		We aim to collect only the minimal amount of information necessary to provide our services:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Account Information:</strong> If you sign in via our central single sign-on (SSO) service, <a href="https://synid.christran.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sYnID</a>, we store your email address and profile identifiers to manage your sessions.</li>
		<li><strong>Cookies:</strong> We use local browser storage and session cookies to keep you signed in across our services.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. Bot Protection & Spam Prevention (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
	<p>
		To protect our login portals, forms, and resource-heavy endpoints (such as AI image generation) from automated bot abuse, 
		spam, and brute-force attacks, we implement <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>.
	</p>
	<p>
		Turnstile operates by evaluating telemetry and behavior data from your browser (including screen characteristics, device features, and IP address) 
		to distinguish human visitors from automated bots without tracking your personal browsing habits.
	</p>
	<p>
		The collection and processing of this data is subject to Cloudflare's privacy policies. For more information, please review the 
		<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Hosting, CDN, Security, and Analytics (Cloudflare Infrastructure)</h2>
	<p>
		Our websites and associated web services are hosted on, routed through, and analyzed using Cloudflare network infrastructure.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Infrastructure & Security:</strong> As a reverse proxy provider, Cloudflare processes network traffic to and from our servers. This includes collecting technical transmission metrics and logs (such as IP addresses, web request details, user-agent headers, and security logs) to optimize performance, protect against DDoS attacks, and safeguard our servers.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Privacy-First Web Analytics:</strong> We utilize Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand our website traffic and improve our services. This analytics tool operates without using any cookies, local storage, or persistent identifiers. It collects only aggregate, non-identifiable data (such as page views, browser types, and general geographic location based on IP address) to provide us with traffic statistics. It does not track your behavior across other websites.
	</p>
	<p>
		All Cloudflare processing is handled for our legitimate business interests in maintaining a secure, performant, and reliable website. For more information, please review the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
	<p>
		Any information collected is used solely to:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Authenticate your user session.</li>
		<li>Prevent abuse, fraud, and server resource depletion.</li>
		<li>Provide the core features of the applications (e.g. saving generated images to your profile gallery).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Contact Us</h2>
	<p>
		If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at:
		<a href="mailto:privacy@christran.io">privacy@christran.io</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
